## Builder notes (not a rating)
Green looked at the four color files and the four line-art files in one montage.
- The nut alone reads as a nut in color and in line art. The cap edge shows one thin dark crease
  line and no scattered black specks. The bottom ends in a point, and the stem leans.
- The nut in Nan's hand reads as an acorn, and the hand stays closed around it. Small dark marks
  show at the outer eye corners.
- On the nest-and-a-nut page, Pip's nose meets the nut on the grass. The low branch is a Y shape
  that reads as a branch, not as a hand. The nest sits in the fork with three eggs.
- On the a-nest page, one straight trunk reads as a tree, not as a lamp post. The nest sits in
  the fork. Nan's held-out hand reads as a mitt.
- No letter, number, or logo shows in any file.

